================================================================================
Annotation data sources
================================================================================
The shipped curated seed (data/seed/associations.json) contains project-authored
educational interpretations of well-replicated variants, drafted with AI assistance
and NOT reviewed by a geneticist or clinician. Each association names the source
database it was drawn from (below), but carries no per-association citation. The
seed does NOT redistribute any third-party dataset file.

NHGRI-EBI GWAS Catalog
    SNP-trait associations. EMBL-EBI Terms of Use; freely reusable with citation.
    Downloaded on-device by `update_databases`. Cite: Sollis et al., the GWAS
    Catalog. https://www.ebi.ac.uk/gwas/

NCBI ClinVar
    Clinical significance of variants. Public domain (U.S. Government work).
    Downloaded on-device by `update_databases`. Cite: Landrum et al., ClinVar.
    https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/clinvar/

ClinPGx (formerly PharmGKB)
    Pharmacogenomics. PharmGKB merged into ClinPGx (with CPIC and PharmCAT) in
    July 2025; pharmgkb.org URLs now redirect to clinpgx.org. The licence did not
    change with the rebrand, and attribution is still owed to PharmGKB by name.
    Licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 (copyleft), per the LICENSE.txt shipped inside the data
    download itself, which additionally requires that:
      - recipients of any altered/reused PharmGKB data first agree to the same
        licence, and proof of that agreement be made available to PharmGKB; and
      - "Under no circumstances can PharmGKB data be sold for other's private or
        commercial use."
    NOT redistributed with this software: it is downloaded onto the user's own
    machine by `update_databases`, stored in its own source partition, and shown
    with CC BY-SA 4.0 + PharmGKB attribution in-app. Any redistribution of a
    PharmGKB-derived dataset must comply with CC BY-SA 4.0 and those terms.
    Cite: https://www.clinpgx.org/page/citingPharmgkb
    https://www.clinpgx.org/

dbSNP / Ensembl (build-time support only)
    rsID normalization and GRCh37/GRCh38 coordinates. dbSNP: public domain (NCBI).
    Ensembl: no data-reuse restriction (EMBL-EBI). Used once, at build time, to
    enrich the seed coordinates (scripts/enrich_seed_coords.py). Never contacted
    at runtime and never sent any user data. Cite dbSNP and Ensembl.

No user genetic data is ever collected, stored, transmitted, or used to train
anything. All parsing and annotation happen locally on your device.
